This one is a bit strange and has a type error at it's call-site. The type here [is MessageContent](https://github.com/nperez0111/continue/blob/8b11e1009497a50973464b2c0c4353d7fa59bc00/core/index.d.ts#L181) but, it seems that this code only ever assumes streamUpdate to be called with a string. So this change exposed a type incompatibility that I wasn't sure how you guys wanted to resolve. I wrote up how I'd resolve this in my suggestion. But I don't know how you guys were planning on outputting image urls (the text case is straightforward of course.


```suggestion
    streamUpdate: (
      state,
      action: PayloadAction<ChatHistoryItem["message"]["content"]>
    ) => {
      if (state.history.length) {
        const historyItem = state.history[state.history.length - 1];
        if (typeof action.payload === "string") {
          historyItem.message.content += action.payload;
        } else {
          historyItem.message.content += action.payload
            .map((message) => {
              if (message.type === "text") {
                return message.text;
              }
              if (message.type === "imageUrl") {
                return message.imageUrl.url;
              }
              return "";
            })
            .join();
        }
      }
    },
```

